  "worked_solution": "The set $Y-X$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Y$ but *not* $X.$ Note that the elements $1,3\\in X$ are also in $Y,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y-X & ={1,2,3,4}-{1,3,5,7} \\\\  & ={2,4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
